[
    {
        "id": "chrome",
        "name": "Chrome & Edge",
        "category": "browser",
        "description": "Browser frame, tab strip, toolbar and new tab page colors for Chromium browsers.",
        "homepage": "https://www.google.com/chrome",
        "tags": [
            "chromium",
            "edge",
            "brave",
            "vivaldi",
            "browser"
        ],
        "install": "\n1. Open `chrome://extensions` (or `edge://extensions`) and enable **Developer mode**.\n2. **Load unpacked** → select `dist/dark` or `dist/light`.\n\nChrome keeps one theme at a time; loading the other replaces it.\n",
        "status": "available",
        "source": "https://github.com/repraze/termicolor/tree/main/ports/chrome",
        "files": [
            "dark/manifest.json",
            "light/manifest.json"
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "shiki",
        "name": "Shiki & Monaco",
        "category": "web",
        "description": "Syntax highlighting themes for shiki (and Monaco via @shikijs/monaco). Same token rules as VS Code.",
        "homepage": "https://shiki.style",
        "tags": [
            "syntax",
            "highlight",
            "monaco",
            "textmate",
            "markdown",
            "code blocks"
        ],
        "install": "\nThe files are TextMate themes - load them directly:\n\n```ts\nimport termicolorDark from \"./termicolor-dark.json\";\nimport termicolorLight from \"./termicolor-light.json\";\n\nconst highlighter = await createHighlighter({themes: [termicolorDark, termicolorLight], langs: [\"ts\"]});\nhighlighter.codeToHtml(code, {lang: \"ts\", themes: {light: \"termicolor-light\", dark: \"termicolor-dark\"}});\n```\n\nFor Monaco, register the same themes through `shikiToMonaco(highlighter, monaco)`.\n",
        "status": "available",
        "source": "https://github.com/repraze/termicolor/tree/main/ports/shiki",
        "files": [
            "termicolor-dark.json",
            "termicolor-light.json"
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "starship",
        "name": "Starship",
        "category": "shell",
        "description": "Palette blocks and a rainbow powerline preset for the Starship prompt.",
        "homepage": "https://starship.rs",
        "tags": [
            "prompt",
            "powerline",
            "bash",
            "zsh",
            "fish",
            "powershell"
        ],
        "install": "\n**Full preset:** copy `starship-dark.toml` (or `-light`) to `~/.config/starship.toml`.\nNeeds a [Nerd Font](https://www.nerdfonts.com).\n\n**Palette only:** append `palettes.toml` to your config and set `palette = 'termicolor_dark'`.\nColors: `red orange yellow green cyan blue purple pink text subtext surface base crust`.\n",
        "status": "available",
        "source": "https://github.com/repraze/termicolor/tree/main/ports/starship",
        "files": [
            "starship-dark.toml",
            "starship-light.toml",
            "palettes.toml"
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "vscode",
        "name": "Visual Studio Code",
        "category": "editor",
        "description": "Dark and light color themes for VS Code and VSCodium, matching repraze.com code blocks.",
        "homepage": "https://code.visualstudio.com",
        "tags": [
            "vscodium",
            "cursor",
            "editor",
            "monaco"
        ],
        "install": "\nNot on the Marketplace yet. Package and install the extension folder:\n\n```sh\ncd ports/vscode/dist\nnpx @vscode/vsce package -o termicolor.vsix\ncode --install-extension termicolor.vsix\n```\n\nThen pick **Termicolor Dark** or **Termicolor Light** in *Preferences: Color Theme*.\n",
        "status": "available",
        "source": "https://github.com/repraze/termicolor/tree/main/ports/vscode",
        "files": [
            "package.json",
            "README.md",
            "LICENSE",
            "themes/termicolor-dark.json",
            "themes/termicolor-light.json"
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "windows-terminal",
        "name": "Windows Terminal",
        "category": "terminal",
        "description": "Color schemes plus a matching window/tab theme for Windows Terminal.",
        "homepage": "https://github.com/microsoft/terminal",
        "tags": [
            "windows",
            "wt",
            "ansi"
        ],
        "install": "\n**Option A - fragment (auto-loads):** copy `termicolor.json` to\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft\\Windows Terminal\\Fragments\\termicolor\\termicolor.json` and restart.\nThe schemes appear in *Settings → Color schemes*.\n\n**Option B - settings.json:** paste the objects from `schemes.json` into `\"schemes\"` and from\n`themes.json` into `\"themes\"`. Then set:\n\n```json\n\"profiles\": {\"defaults\": {\"colorScheme\": \"Termicolor Dark\"}},\n\"theme\": \"Termicolor Dark\"\n```\n",
        "status": "available",
        "source": "https://github.com/repraze/termicolor/tree/main/ports/windows-terminal",
        "files": [
            "termicolor.json",
            "schemes.json",
            "themes.json"
        ]
    },
